  "what_this_state_establishes": {
    "establishes": [
      "The published Study 4F instrument binds byte-exactly at 5fd9602df207e95789263d0f8d52428540f48fb8: all fifteen decision-bearing files and all thirteen registered semantic invariants were reconfirmed without modifying anything.",
      "On the authenticated Azure identity available to this successor, both registered accelerator SKUs are offered broadly and neither carries a NotAvailableForSubscription restriction, so SKU availability and Azure Policy are not the blocking dimension.",
      "The blocking dimension is VM-family vCPU quota: the StandardNCadsH100v5Family and StandardNCADSA100v4Family limits are zero in every region returned for the respective SKU, while the total-regional vCPU limit of 100 would have admitted one instance.",
      "Exactly one minimal quota request was submitted, for exactly one instance of the first eligible SKU/region, and the quota service refused it with QuotaNotAvailableForResource. The family limit remains zero.",
      "No prohibited workaround was taken: no quantization, no sharding, no CPU or disk offload, no device_map='auto', no Spot capacity, no ineligible accelerator substitution and no enlarged quota request."
    ],
    "does_not_establish": [
      "Nothing about Azure GPU capacity, which was never observed because section 4.1 forbids provisioning without quota. Capacity is unknown, not unavailable.",
